   "rod_through_hand": "per sample, for each rail/rung axis clipped to the hand bbox + 1 cm (so the clipped axis starts and ends outside the hand): exact segment-triangle intersection against every Hand-bone triangle, then the generalized winding number at the midpoint of each interval between crossings. FLAG if the axis crosses the hand skin at all, or any interval is inside a closed hand piece (|w| > 0.5). A wrapped grip leaves the axis in the palm/finger cavity with 0 crossings; a rod through the hand (incl. through the back of the glove) must cross the skin. Reports solid inside length and samples where only zero-thickness (double-sided) hand faces are crossed."
  },
